title: Judiciary & Intelligence
subtitle: Courts, investigations and the Senate Bureau of Intelligence.
is-card: true
tags: senate_affairs
card-image: img/card_law.svg
view-if: judiciary_timer <= 0 and chair_judiciary = "rc" and cardok_judiciary
on-arrival: turn_actions += 1; judiciary_timer = 3; last_card_timer = "judiciary"
new-page: true

= Judiciary & Intelligence Committee

The Caucus chairs the Judiciary & Intelligence Committee: the Republic's courts, the Judicial Department and the Senate Bureau of Intelligence answer to it.

- @prosecute: Prosecute corruption.
- @ethics: Establish a Senate Ethics Commission.
- @intel: Order an intelligence review of the Chancellery's contacts.
- @gunray: Press the case against Nute Gunray.
- @warrant: Prepare a Senate warrant for the Sith Lord.
- @bureau_reform: Reform the Senate bureaucracy.
- @easy_discard

@prosecute
view-if: corruption > 20
subtitle: −3 corruption; some blocs feel targeted.
on-arrival: corruption -= 3; mod_relation -= 3; guild_relation -= 3; faith += 0.5

Twelve senators and forty officials are indicted for bribery. Several of them were Caucus allies.

@ethics
view-if: not anti_corruption
subtitle: −1 political capital. A permanent safeguard against corruption, if the Senate agrees.
choose-if: capital >= 1 and rc_in_govt
unavailable-subtitle: Needs 1 political capital and a seat in government.
on-arrival: {!
Q.capital -= 1;
var st = SW.stance(Q, {mod: 0.55, guild: 0.15, rim: 0.7, sec: 0.45, ind: 0.55, pal: 0.45, cis: 0.3}, true);
Q.eth_vote = SW.vote(Q, st, 1, ['oversight', 'regulate']);
Q.vote_html = SW.voteBanner('Senate Ethics Commission Act', Q.eth_vote);
if (Q.eth_vote >= 50) { Q.anti_corruption = 1; Q.corruption -= 4; Q.faith += 2; }
!}

[+ vote_html +]

[? if anti_corruption : The Senate Ethics Commission is born, with real powers of audit. Corruption will be harder from now on. ?][? if not anti_corruption : Too many senators have too much to hide. The bill fails. ?]

@intel
view-if: intel_runs < 3
subtitle: +1 evidence. The Chancellery may notice.
on-arrival: {! Q.evidence += 1; Q.intel_runs += 1; if (Math.random() < 0.15 + Q.grand_plan / 500) Q.leak_pending = 1; !}

The Bureau's analysts map the Chancellery's contacts. A disturbing number of them lead to people who later died, disappeared or became very rich.

@gunray
view-if: gunray_stage >= 1 and gunray_stage <= 4 and not gunray_convicted
subtitle: Strengthens the prosecution at the next trial.
on-arrival: gunray_bonus += 1

The Judiciary Committee assigns its best prosecutors to the Gunray case and shields the witnesses.

@warrant
view-if: evidence >= 7 and not warrant
subtitle: [? if evidence >= 8 : Our evidence can justify a warrant. ?][? if evidence < 8 : We need a little more before a judge will sign. ?]
choose-if: evidence >= 8
unavailable-subtitle: Needs compelling evidence (8+).
on-arrival: warrant = 1; senate_resolve += 0.5

A sealed warrant is drafted and signed by three justices of the Supreme Court. It names no one yet. It does not need to. If the moment comes, the Jedi will be acting for the Senate, not against it.

@bureau_reform
view-if: bureau_reform_timer <= 0 and bureau_relation < 70
subtitle: −2 political capital. Clears out the guilds' placemen: the bureaucracy warms to us considerably, the guilds less so.
choose-if: capital >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: Needs 2 political capital.
on-arrival: capital -= 2; bureau_relation += 30; guild_relation -= 5; inst_dissent -= 3; bureau_reform_timer = 6

The Committee audits the Senate's payroll. Forty officials on retainer to the Trade Federation are quietly retired; their replacements owe their jobs to the reform. For a while, at least, the Caucus's bills reach the floor on time.
